      "refersTo": "station-line",
      "description": "The signature 2px rail: orange traveled segment, solid done stations, ringed current, hollow ahead.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-line\"><span class=\"ds-rail\"></span><span class=\"ds-rail-done\" style=\"width:66.6%\"></span><span class=\"ds-st ds-done\"></span><span class=\"ds-st ds-done\"></span><span class=\"ds-st ds-current\"></span><span class=\"ds-st ds-ahead\"></span></div><div class=\"ds-line-labels\"><span>Start</span><span>Checkpoint</span><span>Poll</span><span>Reflection</span></div>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-line{position:relative;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;height:16px;width:320px;} .ds-rail,.ds-rail-done{position:absolute;left:0;top:50%;height:2px;transform:translateY(-50%);} .ds-rail{right:0;background:var(--line-strong);} .ds-rail-done{background:var(--accent);transition:width .7s var(--ease-out-expo);} .ds-st{position:relative;width:14px;height:14px;border-radius:9999px;border:2px solid;box-sizing:border-box;} .ds-done{border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--accent);} .ds-current{border-color:var(--accent);background:var(--bg);box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgb(238 66 22/.2);} .ds-ahead{border-color:var(--line-strong);background:var(--bg);} .ds-line-labels{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;width:320px;margin-top:12px;font:400 .75rem 'Geist',sans-serif;color:var(--subtle);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Line Bullet",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "line-bullet",
      "description": "36px circle with a two-letter course code in Geist Mono, outline or solid ink.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-bullet\">EL</span> <span class=\"ds-bullet ds-bullet-solid\">HB</span>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-bullet{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:9999px;border:2px solid var(--fg);color:var(--fg);box-sizing:border-box;font:500 .72rem 'Geist Mono',ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:-.025em;} .ds-bullet-solid{background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Checkpoint Card",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card",
      "description": "Front of a checkpoint: raised hairline card, prompt, answer options, with offset deck edges beneath.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-deck\"><div class=\"ds-edge ds-edge-violet\"></div><div class=\"ds-edge ds-edge-raised\"></div><div class=\"ds-card\"><p class=\"ds-kind\"><b>Checkpoint</b>, from The Elephant and the Rider</p><p class=\"ds-prompt\">A bat and a ball cost $1.10. How much is the ball?</p><button class=\"ds-opt\">10 cents <svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z\"/></svg></button><button class=\"ds-opt\">5 cents <svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z\"/></svg></button></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-deck{position:relative;width:340px;padding-bottom:12px;} .ds-edge{position:absolute;height:100%;border-radius:16px;} .ds-edge-violet{left:24px;right:24px;bottom:0;background:var(--violet);} .ds-edge-raised{left:12px;right:12px;bottom:6px;background:var(--raised);border:1px solid var(--line);} .ds-card{position:relative;border-radius:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--raised);padding:24px;color:var(--fg);} .ds-kind{margin:0;font:400 .875rem 'Geist',sans-serif;color:var(--subtle);} .ds-kind b{font-weight:500;color:var(--fg);} .ds-prompt{margin:10px 0 18px;font:600 1.25rem/1.375 'Geist',sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;} .ds-opt{display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:8px;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);background:transparent;color:var(--fg);font:500 1rem 'Geist',sans-serif;cursor:pointer;transition:border-color .15s,background-color .15s;} .ds-opt svg{color:var(--subtle);} .ds-opt:hover{border-color:var(--fg);background:rgb(17 16 28/.03);} .ds-opt:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus);outline-offset:2px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Answered Card Back",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "card-back",
      "description": "The violet answered side: verdict, explanation in muted lilac, and the way forward.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-back\"><p class=\"ds-verdict\">Right. Your slow system stepped in.</p><p class=\"ds-expl\">Most people say 10 cents first. That quick answer is your fast, intuitive system talking.</p><div class=\"ds-back-foot\"><span>Card 1 of 3</span><button class=\"ds-next\">Next card <svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M221.66,133.66l-72,72a8,8,0,0,1-11.32-11.32L196.69,136H40a8,8,0,0,1,0-16H196.69L138.34,61.66a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32l72,72A8,8,0,0,1,221.66,133.66Z\"/></svg></button></div></div>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-back{width:340px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--violet);color:var(--on-violet);padding:28px;} .ds-verdict{margin:0;font:500 .875rem 'Geist',sans-serif;} .ds-expl{margin:12px 0 0;font:400 1.125rem/1.625 'Geist',sans-serif;color:var(--on-violet-muted);} .ds-back-foot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-top:28px;font:400 .875rem 'Geist',sans-serif;color:var(--on-violet-muted);} .ds-next{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:36px;padding:0 14px;border-radius:10px;border:0;background:var(--on-violet);color:var(--violet);font:500 .875rem 'Geist',sans-serif;cursor:pointer;transition:opacity .15s;} .ds-next:hover{opacity:.9;} .ds-next:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--on-violet);outline-offset:2px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "App Sidebar Nav",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "nav-item-active",
      "description": "8px rows; active row has a 6% ink wash, medium weight and an Orange Ink icon.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-nav-item ds-active\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 256 256\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M104,40H56A16,16,0,0,0,40,56v48a16,16,0,0,0,16,16h48a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V56A16,16,0,0,0,104,40Zm96,0H152a16,16,0,0,0-16,16v48a16,16,0,0,0,16,16h48a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V56A16,16,0,0,0,200,40Zm-96,96H56a16,16,0,0,0-16,16v48a16,16,0,0,0,16,16h48a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V152A16,16,0,0,0,104,136Zm96,0H152a16,16,0,0,0-16,16v48a16,16,0,0,0,16,16h48a16,16,0,0,0,16-16V152A16,16,0,0,0,200,136Z\"/></svg>Dashboard</a><a class=\"ds-nav-item\" href=\"#\">My courses</a><a class=\"ds-nav-item\" href=\"#\">Reflections</a></nav>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-nav{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;width:220px;} .ds-nav-item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:8px 12px;border-radius:8px;font:400 .875rem 'Geist',sans-serif;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color .15s,color .15s;} .ds-nav-item:hover{background:rgb(17 16 28/.04);color:var(--fg);} .ds-nav-item:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--focus);outline-offset:2px;} .ds-active{background:rgb(17 16 28/.06);color:var(--fg);font-weight:500;} .ds-active svg{color:var(--accent-ink);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Badge",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "badge-accent",
      "description": "6px-radius label chip in neutral, accent, violet and soft tones.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-badge ds-b-neutral\">4 lessons</span> <span class=\"ds-badge ds-b-accent\">Free</span> <span class=\"ds-badge ds-b-violet\">+50 XP</span>",
      "css": ":host{--bg:#f8f2ea;--raised:#fffbf6;--sunken:#efe7db;--fg:#11101c;--muted:#4d4859;--subtle:#6a6475;--line:rgb(17 16 28/.12);--line-strong:rgb(17 16 28/.24);--accent:#ee4216;--accent-hover:#d93a10;--accent-ink:#b5300c;--on-accent:#11101c;--violet:#361a6a;--on-violet:#f8f2ea;--on-violet-muted:#cbbfe0;--focus:#361a6a;--ease-out-expo:cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1);font-family:'Geist',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;} .ds-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:6px;font:500 .75rem 'Geist',sans-serif;} .ds-b-neutral{border:1px solid var(--line-strong);color:var(--muted);} .ds-b-accent{background:var(--accent);color:var(--on-accent);} .ds-b-violet{background:var(--violet);color:var(--on-violet);}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Line You Ride",
    "overview": "Pintevact draws learning as a transit line. Every lesson is a line, every checkpoint is a station, and every station is a card you answer. Answering flips the card to its deep violet back and fills the next stretch of rail in signal orange. The whole interface is built from three materials: a warm paper (or night) ground, 2px rails with circle stations, and flat hairline cards. Nothing else is decorative; progress is the ornament.\n\nThe mood is calm precision with a single hot signal: Linear-grade restraint in the chrome, Brilliant-style learning by doing in the content. Density is moderate and editorial on the public site (one idea per section, generous section rhythm) and tighter in the app (dashboard, player, vault), but both share the same tokens, radii and line grammar. Light and dark are equal citizens: the theme is class-driven (`.dark` on `html`), follows the OS setting by default, and has a manual toggle. The lesson player stage is always dark, whatever the page theme.\n\nThe system rejects pastel wellness illustration and the dark neon AI hero, and it replaces a previous look the user rejected as busy and AI-generated.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One accent, signal orange, reserved for the traveled line, finished stations and the primary action.",
      "Deep violet is the answered side of a card and the colour of deep panels; it never appears as a gradient.",
      "Geist Sans for everything; Geist Mono only for line codes and literal code; Outfit caps only for the PINTEVACT wordmark.",
      "2px rails, circle stations: hollow ahead, orange done, ringed current.",
      "Flat hairline cards (16px); stack depth by offset card edges, not drop shadows.",
      "Phosphor icons, regular weight (fill weight marks the active nav item)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Signal Rule",
        "body": "Orange means \"traveled\" or \"go\". It marks the rail you have covered, stations you have filled, and the single primary action in a view. It is never a background wash, a heading colour or a decorative stripe.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Answered Side Rule",
        "body": "Violet means \"answered\" or \"yours\". A surface turns violet when the learner has responded, completed, or earned something; it is not a generic brand panel colour for arbitrary content.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "All labels, card kinds and meta lines are sentence case at normal tracking. Uppercase and wide tracking belong to the wordmark alone.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Any number that changes or sits in a column (time, XP, price, counts, percentages) is set with tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stacked Deck Rule",
        "body": "A card that is part of a sequence shows its depth by the offset edges of the cards behind it, never by a drop shadow. Cards at rest are flat.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Floating-Only Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Shadows are reserved for layers that float over the page (toasts, menus). Cards, panels, buttons and inputs never cast one.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do draw progress as a 2px rail with circle stations: hollow ahead, orange done, ringed current.",
      "Do keep Signal Orange to the traveled line, finished stations and one primary action per view, with Night Ink text on it.",
      "Do flip answered cards to Card-Back Violet and put feedback, XP and the next action on that back.",
      "Do show stack depth with offset card edges beneath the active card.",
      "Do use Geist Sans throughout, tabular figures for every changing number, and sentence case labels.",
      "Do use Orange Ink rather than Signal Orange for small text and icons on the ground, so contrast holds in both themes.",
      "Do keep the lesson player stage dark in both themes, and verify every screen in light and dark.",
      "Do use Phosphor icons at regular weight, inlined at 14 to 20px."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put drop shadows on cards, panels, buttons or inputs; shadows belong only to floating toasts and menus.",
      "Don't use orange or violet as gradients, background washes or decorative stripes.",
      "Don't set the wordmark face, uppercase or wide tracking on anything but PINTEVACT.",
      "Don't introduce a second accent hue, pastel illustration, or neon-on-black hero treatments.",
      "Don't put white text on Signal Orange.",
      "Don't add progress visuals other than the rail (no rings, gauges or chunky bars)."
    ]
  }
}